1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,140
In 1976, two young men had an idea that would eventually change the entire

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:08,520
world. Their names were Steve Jobs and Steve Wozniak.

3
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,040
They weren't billionaires.

4
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:13,740
They didn't have a huge office or a powerful company behind them.

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,640
Just an idea, a garage, and a dream.

6
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:19,620
Steve Wozniak was the engineering genius.

7
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,820
He designed a personal computer called the Apple I.

8
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,960
Steve Jobs saw something bigger.

9
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,820
He believed computers shouldn't just be for scientists and businesses.

10
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:32,800
They should be something ordinary people could use in their own homes.

11
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:36,360
But turning an invention into a business wasn't easy.

12
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,280
They needed money, customers,

13
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,200
and someone willing to believe in them.

14
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,960
So they took a huge risk, sold what they could,

15
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,640
and started building their company.

16
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,160
They even brought in a third co-founder,

17
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:50,840
Ronald Wayne. Then came the Apple II in 1977.

18
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:55,800
It became a major success and helped transform Apple from a small startup

19
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:59,060
into one of the most important technology companies in America.

20
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:03,460
Their little idea was becoming something much bigger than anyone imagined.

21
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:08,200
Years later, Apple would introduce products that changed how people communicate,

22
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,900
listen to music, work, and live.

23
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,680
The iPod, the iPhone, the iPad,

24
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:17,240
and eventually, a company worth trillions of dollars.

25
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:21,600
And it all started with two young men who believe computers could change

26
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,260
the world. because sometimes,

27
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:27,520
the biggest companies on earth begin with nothing more than a small idea.
